 "findings": [
  {
   "evidence": "The two `have`s in the proof only use `(pathLastArrowEquiv i b).symm.injective` into `Path i b` and `sigma_mk_injective`. Mathlib's `Nat.card_prod (\u03b1 \u03b2 : Type*)` is unconditional (Finite.lean:223), and `Nat.card_sigma` needs only `[Fintype \u03b1] [\u2200 a, Finite (\u03b2 a)]` (Finite.lean:234), which the second `have` supplies.",
   "file": "TauCeti/RepresentationTheory/Quiver/LastArrow.lean",
   "fix": "Use `theorem card_path_eq_ite_add_sum_lastArrow [DecidableEq V] [Fintype V] (i b : V) [Finite (Quiver.Path i b)] : ...` and update the docstring to say that finiteness of the paths `i \u2192 b` alone makes the counts honest. Callers holding `\u2200 a` instances still find the instance automatically.",
   "issue": "`[\u2200 a : V, Finite (Quiver.Path i a)]` is only used at `a = b`. The sigma summand's finiteness comes from injecting into `Path i b`, each fibre is finite because it injects into the sigma, and `Nat.card_prod` needs no finiteness. So the lemma is stated more weakly than it could be.",
   "line": 101
  }
 ],
